## 1.3 End-to-End Data Flow

```text
[1]  Recruiter uploads 1000+ PDFs ──► API Gateway (JWT + throttle) ──► Resume Ingestion Service
[2]  Service validates magic bytes, generates batch_id, Redis idempotency SET NX
[3]  Each PDF ──► S3 (pre-signed PUT)  →  s3://resumes/{agency}/{batch_id}/{resume_id}.pdf
[4]  Service publishes N messages ──► resume.ingestion.queue  (one per resume, carries correlation_id)
[5]  Ingestion Worker(s) consume (≤10 concurrent/worker):
        a. Download PDF from S3
        b. PDFLoader → raw text
        c. Section-aware chunking (Skills / Experience / Projects / Achievements)
        d. HuggingFace all-MiniLM-L6-v2 → 384-dim embeddings per chunk
        e. ATOMIC: ChromaDB upsert (idempotent by chunk_id) + PostgreSQL resume_chunks insert
        f. Update resumes.status = 'ingested', emit progress
[6]  When job profile ranking is triggered ──► ranking.job.queue
[7]  Ranking Orchestrator acquires Redis mutex(job_profile_id):
        a. RAG Pipeline Builder ensures collection resumes_job_{id} is current (delta upsert)
        b. For each resume: retrieve top-10 chunks filtered by resume_id
        c. Build weighted prompt (JD + chunks), enqueue into OpenAI Batch
        d. OpenAI GPT-4o ──► ranked JSON (score 0–100, tier, sub-scores, strengths, gaps)
        e. Validate JSON vs schema → store in PostgreSQL match_results (optimistic lock)
        f. Emit ranking:result per resume via Socket.IO; update progress %
[8]  On completion: release mutex ──► publish to excel.export.queue
[9]  Export Worker: ExcelJS streaming writer → 3 sheets → S3 multipart upload (.xlsx)
[10] Publish S3 URL ──► notification.dispatch.queue
[11] Notification Service consumes: pre-signed GET URL → email (SES) + in-app notification row
        → increment Redis notif:unread:{hr_user_id}
[12] Socket.IO emits ranking:complete ──► Next.js dashboard refreshes charts in real time
```

Every message from step [4] onward carries a **correlation_id** so a single resume can be traced across
ingestion → embedding → ranking → export → delivery (see §4.4).

