## 1.8 API Gateway Integration

### Comparison: AWS API Gateway vs Kong

| Criterion | AWS API Gateway | Kong |
|-----------|-----------------|------|
| Hosting | Fully managed (AWS only) | Self-host / Kong Konnect (cloud) |
| JWT validation | Via Lambda authorizer / Cognito | Native JWT plugin |
| Rate limiting | Usage plans + API keys | Rate-limiting plugin (Redis-backed, per-consumer) |
| WebSocket support | Yes (separate WS API) | Yes (native TCP/WS proxy) |
| Plugin ecosystem | Limited to AWS services | Rich OSS plugin ecosystem |
| Portability / lock-in | High AWS lock-in | Cloud-agnostic |
| Cost model | Per-request + data | Infra (OSS free) / subscription |
| Custom logic | Lambda authorizers | Lua/Go/JS plugins |
| Latency | Low (managed edge) | Low (co-located with services) |

### Recommendation: **Kong**

**Justification:** The platform mixes REST + WebSocket (Socket.IO) traffic and needs **Redis-backed,
per-consumer (per-role) rate limiting** and **native JWT validation** — all first-class Kong plugins. Kong is
cloud-agnostic (we deploy via Docker Compose / Kubernetes alongside the services), avoids AWS lock-in, and its
WS proxying integrates cleanly with the Socket.IO server. AWS API Gateway is the better pick only if the org is
strictly AWS-managed-only and already standardised on Cognito.

### Responsibilities
- JWT auth validation (reject before routing upstream).
- Rate limiting per role (Recruiter: 100 req/min, HR viewer: 20 req/min) via the rate-limiting plugin keyed on
  the JWT consumer.
- Request routing to Express services + request schema validation.
- SSL/TLS termination.
- Structured request/response logging (correlation IDs forwarded as `X-Correlation-Id`).

### Throttling
- **Bulk upload endpoint:** max **5 concurrent uploads per agency** enforced via a Kong request-termination /
  rate-limiting plugin keyed on `agency_id`, backed by Redis.

### Usage Plans

| Role | Rate Limit | Burst |
|------|-----------|-------|
| Recruiter | 100 req/min | 20 |
| HR viewer | 20 req/min | 5 |
| AgencyAdmin | 200 req/min | 40 |

