## 4.4 Observability

### Winston structured logger + correlation ID
```js
// logger.js
const winston = require('winston');
const { AsyncLocalStorage } = require('async_hooks');

const als = new AsyncLocalStorage();

const logger = winston.createLogger({
  level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'info',
  format: winston.format.combine(
    winston.format.timestamp(),
    winston.format.errors({ stack: true }),
    winston.format((info) => {
      const store = als.getStore();
      if (store?.correlationId) info.correlationId = store.correlationId;
      info.service = process.env.SERVICE_NAME || 'recruitment';
      return info;
    })(),
    winston.format.json()
  ),
  transports: [new winston.transports.Console()],
});

module.exports = logger;
module.exports.als = als;
```

```js
// middleware/correlation.js
const { v4: uuidv4 } = require('uuid');
const { als } = require('../logger');

function correlationMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] || uuidv4();
  req.correlationId = correlationId;
  res.setHeader('X-Correlation-Id', correlationId);
  als.run({ correlationId }, () => next());
}

module.exports = { correlationMiddleware };
```

### Correlation ID propagation into MQ
Every published message carries `correlationId` in both the AMQP `properties.correlationId` field and the
JSON body (see §3.1, §3.3, §3.10). Workers read it back and run their handler inside
`als.run({ correlationId }, ...)`, so **all** logs for one resume share the same ID end-to-end.

### Key metrics
| Metric | Source | Why |
|--------|--------|-----|
| `queue.depth{queue}` | RabbitMQ mgmt API / Prometheus exporter | autoscale trigger, backpressure |
| `embedding.latency_ms` | ingestion worker timer | detect HF/embedding slowdowns |
| `openai.tokens{model}` | ranking pipeline (response `usage`) | cost tracking + rate budget |
| `ranking.throughput{job}` | results/min counter | SLA on time-to-rank |
| `ingestion.failure_rate` | DLQ rate | data-quality / parsing issues |
| `socket.connections` | Socket.IO gauge | real-time fan-out capacity |
| `excel.export.duration_ms` | export worker timer | export SLA |

Expose via `prom-client` `/metrics` on each service; scrape with Prometheus; dashboard in Grafana; alert on
queue depth, DLQ rate, and OpenAI 429 rate.

